    "https://recruiting.myapps.paychex.com/appone/MainInfoReq.asp?R_ID=7095663&B_ID=91&fid=1&Adid=&SearchScreenID=20139&CountryID=3&LanguageID=2": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Job Information: Graduate Assistant - Blueprint/Honors Program Job Email Opening Apply Now Title Graduate Assistant - Blueprint/Honors Program Description The Blueprint/Honors Program Graduate Assistant is a ten-month position responsible for assisting the Blueprint/Honors Program Director with a variety of tasks to ensure that both programs are operating efficiently and successfully. The Graduate Assistant is expected to maintain office hours while classes are in session. Blueprint Program Review and monitor passport opportunities submitted through Coursedog and schedule passport activities in Handshake. Create QR codes for attendance purposes and email to passport hosts. Communicate passport opportunities to BLU 101 peer leaders and instructors. When possible, attend passport opportunities and other relevant events and document for social media. Assist BLU 201 classes if needed. Other duties as agreed upon Honors Program Assist with record-keeping (monitoring portfolios). Communicate reminders to program members regarding due dates and portfolio updates. Communicate service and other opportunities to program members. Be available to assist students with various Honors-related tasks If available, attend Open House and other recruitment events to promote the Honors Program. Assist with the Student Board. When possible, attend Honors events and document for social media. Other duties as agreed upon Requirements/Qualifications : Enrolled full-time in a Master's or Doctoral program. Graduate of Hilbert College’s Honors Program. Strong written and oral communication skills. TERM : August 1, 2026 - May 31, 2027, 20 hours per week Compensation: $6,000 annual stipend ($3,000 per semester) $3,000 towards the cost of tuition ($1,500 per semester) Free Hilbert College parking pass. Full-Time/Part-Time Part-Time Open Date 3/19/2026 About the Organization Hilbert College, located in suburban Hamburg, N.Y., south of Buffalo, is a private four-year college founded in 1957 in the Catholic Franciscan tradition. Hilbert is a dynamic Western New York college that offers career-focused majors, including one of the top criminal justice programs in the region, and more than 50 minors and concentrations. Hilbert’s personal approach to learning combines liberal arts with an outstanding professionally-focused education that’s taught by professors who bring a depth of real-world experience to the classroom. The college’s engaging, student-centered campus community offers numerous leadership, internship and service learning opportunities from which students launch successful careers while making positive changes in their communities. Hilbert’s Mission: Hilbert College is an independent institution of higher learning that embraces its Catholic Franciscan heritage and values.  Students from diverse backgrounds are educated in liberal arts and professional programs to become informed citizens committed to serving and strengthening their communities. EOE Statement: Hilbert College is an Equal Opportunity Employer and is committed to fostering a diverse community of faculty, staff and students. The College does not discriminate against individuals on the basis of any protected characteristics covered under federal or state law. For more details, see the Colleges policy at https://www.hilbert.edu/about/notice-of-non-discrimination This position is currently accepting applications. Apply Now WE ALSO RECOMMEND Other Jobs Within Same Category -- None found\r\n -- Other Jobs Within 60 Miles Adjunct Instructor - Biology & Chemistry (In-Person) in Hamburg, NY Posted on: 6/16/2023 [Apply Now] Maintenance Technician in Hamburg, NY Posted on: 6/16/2026 [Apply Now] Evening & Weekend Library Associate in Hamburg, NY Posted on: 9/3/2026 [Apply Now] Adjunct Instructor  Behavioral Sciences (Human Services and Psychology) in Hamburg, NY Posted on: 10/21/2025 [Apply Now] Adjunct Instructor  Natural Sciences (Biology, Forensic Biology, and Chemistry) 